{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ds_title","type":"text","text":"# Desloppify\n\n**Type:** Post-hoc codebase quality scanner + cleanup harness\n**Creator:** Pete O'Malley · **Stars:** 2.4K · **v0.9.9**\n**Install:** `pip install --upgrade \"desloppify[full]\"`\n**Languages:** 29 (8 full plugin, 21+ generic via tree-sitter)\n**Stack:** Python 3.11+ · 99.5% Python · 5,367 tests · MIT","x":200,"y":-520,"width":640,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ds_loop_group","type":"group","x":-400,"y":-260,"width":1840,"height":340,"color":"4","label":"Core Loop: scan → plan → next → fix → resolve"},
		{"id":"ds_loop_1","type":"text","text":"## 1. Scan\n\n`desloppify scan --path .`\n\nRuns mechanical detectors:\n- Dead code (tree-sitter)\n- Duplication\n- Cyclomatic complexity\n- Dependency cycles\n- Unused imports/deps\n\nThen LLM subjective review:\n- Naming · Abstraction · Cohesion\n- Module boundaries · Error handling\n\nOutput → language-specific state JSON","x":-380,"y":-210,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ds_loop_2","type":"text","text":"## 2. Plan\n\n`desloppify plan`\n\nReconciles findings into\nprioritized `plan.json`:\n\n- Clusters related issues\n- Separates execution queue\n  from backlog\n- Defers judgment-required\n  issues from auto-clustering\n- Assigns `action_type` and\n  `execution_policy` per cluster\n\nReorderable by human/agent","x":-80,"y":-210,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ds_loop_3","type":"text","text":"## 3. Next\n\n`desloppify next`\n\nDisplays highest-priority item:\n- Which file to change\n- What the issue is\n- Coaching narrative\n- The resolve command to run\n  when done\n\nDraws from execution queue,\nnot backlog\n\n`desloppify backlog` shows\nbroader deferred work","x":220,"y":-210,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ds_loop_4","type":"text","text":"## 4. Fix\n\nAgent or human implements\nthe change:\n\n- Language-specific auto-fixers\n  for supported patterns\n- Manual fix for complex issues\n- LLM-assisted refactoring\n  for subjective findings\n\nEqual effort expected for\nlarge refactors and small fixes\n\nAgent must not substitute\nown analysis for findings","x":520,"y":-210,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ds_loop_5","type":"text","text":"## 5. Resolve\n\n`desloppify resolve fixed <id>`\n`--note 'what changed'`\n`--attest 'I have actually\n[CONCRETE CHANGE] and I am\nnot gaming the score'`\n\nAttestation is mandatory.\nDismissing without fixing\nLOWERS the score.\n\nState updates → score recalc\n→ back to `next`","x":820,"y":-210,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ds_loop_6","type":"text","text":"## Loop\n\n← Repeat from `next`\n\nState persists in\n`.desloppify/` across\nsessions.\n\nCan run for days\nautonomously (v0.8+)\n\nStall detection prevents\ninfinite loops (v0.9.9)\n\nDeleted files auto-resolve","x":1120,"y":-210,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ds_layers_group","type":"group","x":-400,"y":140,"width":900,"height":500,"color":"5","label":"Two Analysis Layers"},
		{"id":"ds_mechanical","type":"text","text":"## Mechanical Detection\n**25% of health score**\n\nDeterministic, tree-sitter-based:\n\n- Dead code (unused functions,\n  classes, variables, imports)\n- Code duplication / copy-paste\n- Cyclomatic complexity\n- Function length\n- Dependency cycles\n- Unreachable code paths\n- Unused dependencies\n\n**Pure functions:**\n`detect_*(data, config) → list[dict]`\nLanguage-agnostic algorithms\nregistered in `base/registry.py`","x":-380,"y":190,"width":420,"height":400,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ds_subjective","type":"text","text":"## Subjective Analysis\n**75% of health score**\n\nLLM-powered, two-phase\n(Observe → Judge pattern):\n\n**Phase 1: Observe**\nLLM reads code without scoring\n(prevents premature anchoring)\n\n**Phase 2: Judge**\nStructured evaluation across:\n- Naming consistency\n- Abstraction appropriateness\n- Module boundary violations\n- Error handling patterns\n- Convention drift\n- Cohesion / responsibility focus\n\nCross-checked against mechanical\nfindings for inconsistency detection","x":60,"y":190,"width":420,"height":400,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ds_scoring_group","type":"group","x":540,"y":140,"width":900,"height":500,"color":"1","label":"Scoring & Anti-Gaming"},
		{"id":"ds_score","type":"text","text":"## Health Score\n\n**75% subjective / 25% mechanical**\n(rebalanced v0.9.5 based on\n200K LOC codebase learnings)\n\n**Thresholds:**\n< 70 = significant issues\n70-90 = functional but sloppy\n90-98 = good engineering\n> 98 = \"a seasoned engineer\n        would respect\"\n\n**Vision:**\nv1.0: score 100 = \"most world-class\nengineers agree is well designed\"\nv2.0: score 100 = \"holistically\nbeautiful\"\n\n**Tiers:** T1 (minor) → T4 (architectural)\nT4 receives highest weight","x":560,"y":190,"width":420,"height":400,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ds_antigaming","type":"text","text":"## Anti-Gaming Mechanisms\n\n**1. Mandatory attestation**\nResolve requires describing\nthe concrete change made\n\n**2. Penalized dismissals**\nDismissing without fixing\n*lowers* the score\n\n**3. Cross-checked assessments**\nSubjective vs mechanical\nfindings validated against\neach other\n\n**4. Persistent state**\n`.desloppify/` prevents\n\"clean scan\" gaming\n\n**5. Numeric target redaction**\nPenalty messages hide targets\nso agents can't reverse-engineer\n\n**6. Judgment exclusion**\nJudgment-required detectors\nexcluded from auto-clustering\n— can't be bulk-resolved","x":1000,"y":190,"width":420,"height":400,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ds_arch_group","type":"group","x":-400,"y":700,"width":900,"height":360,"color":"6","label":"Five-Layer Architecture"},
		{"id":"ds_arch","type":"text","text":"```\nLayer 5: app/           CLI commands\n         ↓ imports\nLayer 4: intelligence/  LLM review,\n         ↓              coaching,\n         ↓              integrity\nLayer 3: languages/     29 plugins\n         ↓              (8 full +\n         ↓              21+ generic)\nLayer 2: engine/        Detectors,\n         ↓              scoring,\n         ↓              planning,\n         ↓              state, queue\nLayer 1: base/          Config, enums,\n                        registry,\n                        discovery\n```\n\nEach layer imports only downward.\nDynamic imports confined to\n`languages/__init__.py` and\n`engine/hook_registry.py`","x":-380,"y":750,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ds_langs","type":"text","text":"## Language Support\n\n**Full plugin** (deep detectors + fixers):\nTypeScript · Python · C# · C++\nDart · GDScript · Go · Rust\n\n**Generic** (linter + tree-sitter):\nRuby · Java · Kotlin · Julia\n+ 18 more auto-discovered\n\n**Per-language:**\n- `LangConfig` — static contract\n  (phases, detectors, thresholds)\n- `LangRun` — mutable runtime\n  (zone maps, dep graphs, complexity)\n- Phases: structural → style → security\n- Each phase: extractors → detectors\n  → normalization","x":60,"y":750,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ds_limits_group","type":"group","x":540,"y":700,"width":900,"height":360,"color":"3","label":"Limitations & Slop Coverage"},
		{"id":"ds_limits","type":"text","text":"## Known Limitations\n\n**Resource intensive**\n1.2M+ tokens, 30+ min on medium codebases\n\n**Churn risk**\nSometimes produces complete rewrites\n\n**State-model coupling**\nRaw issues + derived scoring in single\nmutable doc → non-commutative behavior\n($1K bounty exposed this)\n\n**Itself is AI-generated**\nCreator: \"I didn't write any of the ~91k\nlines and barely understand most of it\"\n\n**No pre-hoc capability**\nPurely reactive — cannot prevent slop\n\n**No harness integration**\nStandalone; needs wrapper for GSD/etc.","x":560,"y":750,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ds_coverage","type":"text","text":"## Slop Types Addressed: 10/18\n\n**Mechanical (6):**\n✅ Dead code · ✅ Duplicates\n✅ God functions · ✅ Dep cycles\n✅ Unused imports (partial)\n✅ Placeholder/stub (partial)\n\n**Subjective (4):**\n✅ Over-engineering (partial)\n✅ Naming drift · ✅ Arch erosion\n✅ Error handling patterns\n\n**Not addressed (8):**\n❌ Verbose comments\n❌ Silent scope expansion\n❌ Cross-language contamination\n❌ Data model mismatches\n❌ Meaningless tests\n❌ Lint suppression\n❌ Outdated/deprecated APIs\n❌ Hallucinated packages (registry)","x":1000,"y":750,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ds_gsd","type":"text","text":"### GSD Integration Potential: Covers S9 (partial) + S10 (full) of the 13-improvement de-sloppification proposal · Can serve as the engine behind `/gsd:slop-check` (heuristic layer) and `/gsd:desloppify` (cleanup command) · Does NOT address S1-S8 improvements (quality stack detection, ANTI-SLOP.md, duplication scanner, plan-checker gates, hooks, executor injection) · Those 8 pre-hoc and ad-hoc improvements remain GSD-specific work","x":-400,"y":1120,"width":1840,"height":80,"color":"4"}
	],
